    "label": "companion-cursor-read-delay-slot",
    "observedEffect": "Both selected-input PURE_C sources emit the complete 1300-byte owner with the 104-byte frame and 100 relocations. Their scheduler dumps place the immediate 20 after the first phase load; at delay-slot filling the volatile read control pulls 20 into the first JAL delay slot. Reading through D_800E9BA0 instead fills the slot with 0xE7000000 and leaves 20 at the expected phase-load position. This fixes one scheduling rotation occupying 70 projected words, preserves all 23 direct cursor writes by the owner, and gives zero word differences across the full projection.",
